  "notes": "Cash-basis village. Governmental lines from the p4 Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances (Total column); the statement rolls forward fund balance, so beginning/ending go to *_fund_balance; cash fields left null as in FY2023-FY2025 (cash lines are on the p3 balance sheet: cash 94,608.94, county treasurer 1,579.86). Interest income 481.83 is printed under Other Financing Sources (Uses), so it is other_financing (as in FY2024); transfers in/out 5.00 from the Total column. Taxes: Other kept as other (p2 Homestead/other is a mixed label). Charges for services 2,828.69 is omitted on p4 but included in its total; taken from the p10 comparative governmental statement. Business-type from the p6 proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Net Position (Total column), measure cash (cash-basis net position = cash + CDs), as in FY2023/FY2024; no single printed total, so receipts = operating revenues + interest; disbursements = 320,170.16 printed on p2. Sewer 'Other' 66,903.59 is printed on p2 as Operating Grants and Contributions, so recorded as donations/contributions (grantor not printed). Water/Sewer transfers 76,150.15 net to zero in the Total column (transfers_net null; per-fund lines in detail). proprietary null (cash basis, as in later years). The only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budget statement p9 (combined), so detail is one line per fund column of the p4 and p6 statements. p10/p11 are comparative copies of the statements (p10 ties to p4; p11 differs from p6, see report_discrepancies). Balance sheet: governmental lines from the p3 governmental funds statement (totals equal the government-wide governmental column p1), business-type lines from the p1 Proprietary column. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
